[note] EXP_SUCCESS is gated on the measured effect (A: a file created at an
       attacker-chosen path through the unmodified service's own REST API).
       B is reported as observed: the asyncpg startup packet reached the
       attacker listener (8 bytes), proving the engine dials the host:port the
       URL named. SQL_REACHES_ATTACKER_CONNECTION = False because the captured
       payload was the startup packet only - the fixed PRAGMA rides the SQLite
       path, not the PostgreSQL handshake. This is stated as measured, not
       extrapolated.
